    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d914">

                <pb facs="0816" n="804" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg804"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.248/823: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-12-30T12:00:00+02:00">December 30,
                            1942—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 9:46 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1373. The following telegram has been sent to the Legation at Cairo.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>December 30, noon. Your December 29, 9 a.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d914-f1"/>
                    </p>
                    <p>I see no present necessity for sending another B–24 to Turkey in substitution
                        for the Liberator that is damaged at Aleppo provided our Army authorities in
                        Cairo can give me definite assurances that the repairs to the damaged plane
                        will actually be completed within 30 days and the plane returned at once
                        thereafter to Eskisehir.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d914-f2"/>
                    </p>
                    <p>Repeated to Department.</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d914-f1" n="2" xml:id="d914-f1-content">
                <p>See <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d914-f2" n="3" xml:id="d914-f2-content">
                <p>After being repaired the plane was returned to Turkey by a civilian crew in March
                    1943.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
